sult { allowed: boolean; limit: number; remaining: number; retryAfterMs: number; } Export interface RateLimitHeaders { 'RateLimit-Limit': string; 'RateLimit-Remaining': string; 'RateLimit-Reset': string; 'Retry-After'?: string; } Ensure windowMs > 0 and maxRequests > 0. keyPrefix defaults to 'rl' if not provided.\"},{\"title\":\"Implement Sliding Window Lua Script\",\"description\":\"FILE: src/lua/slidingWindow.lua — Define the atomic Lua script executed in Redis. KEYS[1] = rate limit key (e.g., rl:user:123). ARGV[1] = current timestamp in ms, ARGV[2] = window start timestamp in ms (now - windowMs), ARGV[3] = unique request ID (now + random), ARGV[4] = max requests, ARGV[5] = TTL in ms (windowMs * 2 for safety). ALGORITHM: 1) ZREMRANGEBYSCORE KEYS[1] '-inf' ARGV[2] (remove expired entries). 2) ZCARD KEYS[1] (count current window entries). 3) If count < ARGV[4]: ZADD KEYS[1] ARGV[1] ARGV[3], EXPIRE KEYS[1] ARGV[5], return {1, ARGV[4] - count - 1, 0, ARGV[4]}. 4) Else: EXPIRE KEYS[1] ARGV[5], calculate retryAfterMs = ZRANGE KEYS[1] 0 0 WITHSCORES (get oldest entry timestamp) + windowMs - now, return {0, 0, retryAfterMs, ARGV[4]}. Return format is an array of integers/strings representing [allowed, remaining, retryAfterMs, limit].\"},{\"title\":\"Implement Rate Limiter Core Module\",\"description\":\"FILE: src/rateLimiter.ts — Export class SlidingWindowRateLimiter. Constructor: constructor(redis: Redis, config: RateLimiterConfig). Method: async check(userKey: string): Promise<RateLimitResult>. Logic: 1) Generate unique request ID using crypto.randomUUID() or timestamp+random. 2) Calculate timestamps (now, windowStart). 3) Execute the Lua script via redis.eval(slidingWindowLua, 1, key, now, windowStart, reqId, config.maxRequests, ttl). 4) Map Lua integer array result to RateLimitResult. ERROR HANDLING: Wrap redis.eval in try/catch. On ANY Redis error (connection, timeout, NOSCRIPT), log the error to stderr, and FAIL OPEN by returning { allowed: true, limit: config.maxRequests, remaining: config.maxRequests - 1, retryAfterMs: 0 }. This ensures Redis outages do not block legitimate traffic.\"},{\"title\":\"Implement Express Middleware Factory\",\"description\":\"FILE: src/middleware.ts — Import SlidingWindowRateLimiter, RateLimiterConfig, RateLimitHeaders. Export function createRateLimiterMiddleware(config: RateLimiterConfig): RequestHandler. Logic: Instantiate SlidingWindowRateLimiter once during middleware initialization. Return an Express middleware async function (req, res, next). 1) Key Extraction: const identifier = req.user?.id ?? req.ip ?? req.socket.remoteAddress. If no identifier found, immediately next(new Error('Rate limit identifier missing')). 2) Construct composite key: ${config.keyPrefix}:${identifier}. 3) Await limiter.check(compositeKey). 4) If result.allowed === false: set headers (RateLimit-Limit, RateLimit-Remaining, RateLimit-Reset = now + result.retryAfterMs, Retry-After = Math.ceil(result.retryAfterMs / 1000)). Respond with res.status(429).json({ error: 'Too Many Requests', retryAfter: result.retryAfterMs }). Do NOT call next(). 5) If result.allowed === true: set standard headers (RateLimit-Limit, RateLimit-Remaining, RateLimit-Reset = now + config.windowMs). Call next(). EDGE CASE: Ensure headers are set before calling next() or res.send() so downstream errors don't prevent header injection.\"},{\"title\":\"Integration and Edge Case Configuration\",\"description\":\"FILE: src/index.ts — Export a ready-to-use Express app example demonstrating proper middleware order. 1) Must use express.json() and authentication middleware BEFORE rate limiter so req.user is populated. 2) Demonstrate mounting: app.use('/api', createRateLimiterMiddleware({ windowMs: 60000, maxRequests: 100 })). 3) Trust Proxy: If deployed behind a load balancer (LB), app.set('trust proxy', true) must be configured so req.ip reflects the LB-forwarded IP (X-Forwarded-For), otherwise all users share the LB's IP. 4) Handle uncaught exceptions and u